          <p>
            <strong>Remember:</strong> respectful friendship does not mean agreeing with
            everything. It means allowing two people to have different experiences without
            turning those differences into personal attacks.
          </p>

          <h2>3. Understanding Cultural Communication Styles</h2>

          <p>
            Different cultures communicate in unique ways. Some value direct speech, while others
            prefer subtle hints. Understanding these differences helps you adapt and communicate
            more effectively.
          </p>

          <h3>High-Context vs. Low-Context Cultures</h3>

          <p>
            Communication researchers sometimes use the terms <strong>high-context</strong> and
            <strong>low-context</strong> to describe differences in how much meaning is communicated
            through surrounding context versus explicit words. These concepts can be useful for
            understanding communication patterns, but they should not be treated as fixed labels
            for every person in a country.
          </p>

