          <h3>Developing Emotional Intelligence</h3>

          <p>
            When you interact with people from diverse backgrounds, you learn to handle different
            emotions, expectations, and communication styles. Over time, you become more patient,
            understanding, and emotionally intelligent.
          </p>

          <h2>Conclusion: Building a World of Respectful Friendships</h2>

          <p>
            Making friends online respectfully across cultures is both an art and a skill. It
            requires awareness, empathy, and consistency — but the rewards are immense. Every
            conversation can teach you something new about humanity, tolerance, and kindness.
          </p>

          <p>
            Online platforms can make it easier to meet people outside your usual social
            environment. Whether you are practicing a language, learning about another culture,
            or simply having a conversation, the same principle applies: curiosity works best when
            it is combined with respect and healthy boundaries.
          </p>

          <p>
            Be curious, not judgmental. Be friendly, not forceful. Listen more than you speak. And
            above all — treat every person you meet online as a potential teacher of life.
          </p>

